# The library's checks, minus what example code does on purpose: printf output, long main()s,
# plain data structs, literal data, a plain enum. Names follow the user conventions here, so the library's
# naming check is off too. A model's sets and variable families are const members: built once, in
# the initializer list, and never assigned - what avoid-const-or-ref-data-members warns about is the point.
# The same identity as tests/docs/.clang-tidy, the code the documentation shows: change the two together.
InheritParentConfig: true
Checks: >
  -readability-identifier-naming,
  -cppcoreguidelines-pro-type-vararg,
  -cppcoreguidelines-avoid-do-while,
  -readability-simplify-boolean-expr,
  -readability-function-cognitive-complexity,
  -misc-non-private-member-variables-in-classes,
  -cppcoreguidelines-non-private-member-variables-in-classes,
  -modernize-use-designated-initializers,
  -readability-magic-numbers,
  -cppcoreguidelines-avoid-magic-numbers,
  -cppcoreguidelines-avoid-const-or-ref-data-members,
  -performance-enum-size
